  "Id": 3069,
  "Title": "Introducing the Provost \u200bExperiential Learning Fund Programme\u200b\u200b\u200b",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "The Office of Student Experience held a townhall for students from all three entities that introduced the PELFP in great detail",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassB1B1BB9777EA4C90B0B4F22C317AE8D2\"><p>\u200bThe Office of Student Experience conducted its first townhall of 2023 for students of AKU's Medical College, School of Nursing and Midwifery, and Institute of Educational Development&#160;with over 300 students were in attendance.&#160;Dr. Laila Akbarali, Interim&#160;Vice Provost - Student Affairs and Services and University Registrar, conducted the townhall and introduced the \u200b<a href=\"/students/pelfp/Pages/home.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">Provost Experiential Learning Fund Programme</a>\u200b\u200b\u200b. Danish Imtiaz, Associate Director, Student Experience, gave an overview of the program along with the eligibility criteria.<br></p><p>The&#160;Registrar's office addressed&#160;the updated policy on outstanding accounts with&#160;the university along with the launch of the online facilitation system for student services. Students were invited to&#160;\u200bvoice their questions and concerns as the townhall wrapped up with a promise to conduct more in the future.&#160;<br></p></div>",
